{title: Hes Still Working On Me}
{key: F}

{comment: Chorus}
[F]He's still [D7]workin' on [Gm7]me,
To [C7]make me what I ought to [F]be.
It took Him just a [D7]week to make the [Gm]moon and the stars,
The [C7]sun and the earth and [F]Jupiter and Mars.
How loving and [D7]patient He must [Gm7]be,
[F/C]He's still [C7]workin' on [F]me!

{comment: Verse 1}
[F]There really ought to be a [C]sign upon my heart,
"[Gm]Don't judge me [C7]yet, there's an [F]unfinished part."
But I'll be perfect, just ac[Gm]cording to His plan,
[F/C]Fashioned by the [C7]Master's loving [F]hand.

{comment: Verse 2}
[F]In the mirror of His Word, [C]reflections that I see
[Gm]Make me wonder why [C7]He never [F]gave up on me.
He loves me as I am, and helps [Gm]me when I pray,
[F/C]Remember He's the [C7]Potter, I'm the [F]clay.
